+## Migration verification
+
+Each authorized PR adds only its tables/constraints and a single linear Alembic revision. PostgreSQL 18.x tests cover fresh DB→head, frozen Phase 1 `0018`→head, invalid legacy state fail-closed preflight, constraints under concurrency, frozen-state UPDATE/DELETE rejection and a data-preserving downgrade refusal. No migration rewrites Phase 1 canonical rows. Exact column/index names may use the repository's established naming convention, but their semantics, types, keys and checks above are fixed; a semantic change requires ADR and revised contract before code.
